WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.290
Meet Bramble, your agent.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.420
It carries every instruction you give it.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.850
One day it forgets to cite a source.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.920
So someone adds a rule.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.350
And another.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.950
And another.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.750
Now nobody knows which rocks still do anything.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.850
Preceptor starts from the mistake that actually happened.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.910
It writes one small cue, and keeps it out of the pack.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.710
Then it races two Brambles on the same tasks.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.250
One gets the cue.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.510
One doesn’t.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.200
Too close to call.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.960
So the cue stays a candidate, and nothing gets added.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.430
Taking a rule out needs proof too.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.150
It goes quiet first.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.410
If the mistake returns, the rule comes back.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.440
Preceptor.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.330
Keep agent guidance that earns its place.
